<title>USA: First Midwest places vice chairman on leave.</title>
<headline>First Midwest places vice chairman on leave.</headline>
<dateline>STORM LAKE, Iowa 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Midwest Financial Inc said on Wednesday that vice chairman and senior vice president Steven Myers has been placed on administrative leave of absence for personal reasons.</p>
<p>James Haahr, chairman, president and chief executive officer for First Midwest Financial and First Federal Savings Bank of the Midwest will assume the duties and responsibilities currently performed by Myers, the compamny said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
